<title>USA: ADR REPORT - Barrick stands out in NY trade.</title>
<headline>ADR REPORT - Barrick stands out in NY trade.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian mining company Barrick Gold Corp stood out in otherwise quiet trade in American Depositary Receipts (ADRs) on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Analysts said ADR volume reflected the slowness of the larger New York market as traders headed into the Thanksgiving Day holiday.</p>
<p>&quot;It's very quiet today. There are no major stories,&quot; said Andrew Melinek, head of ADR research and sales at NatWest Securities.</p>
</text>
